D. THE DEFLECTION PER LINK AND ITS SUM ALONG THE PATH, UNDER EACH WORD (derived; k = (n / d) x the count at the Node)
   closed forms (the continuum, one source of q rows per interval on the full fan, the path from x = -L to +L, L = 26):
   the age word as light's index, n = 1 + f k_a, k_a = (n / d) A, A = 3 q / (4 pi r):
     the turn per Link  d theta / dl = f grad_perp k_a = f k_a(b) b / (b^2 + x^2)^(3 / 2)
     the sum             theta = 2 f k_a(b) L / sqrt(L^2 + b^2)  ->  2 f k_a(b) as L -> infinity: the form M / b; f = 1 Newton's half, f = 2 Einstein's
     the delay per Link  f k_a(x) / c intervals per Link beyond the flight's;  the sum (f k_a(b) b / c) 2 asinh(L / b) = (f k_a(b) b / c) ln(4 L^2 / b^2) (1 + O(b^2 / L^2)): Shapiro's logarithm
   the presence word as light's index, n = 1 + f k_s, k_s = (n / d) P, P = q / (4 pi c r^2):
     the turn per Link  f grad_perp k_s = 2 f k_s(b) b^2 / (b^2 + x^2)^2;  the sum -> pi f k_s(b): the form M / b^2, NOT nature's
     the delay           (f k_s(b) b / c) x pi: the form M / b, NOT Shapiro's logarithm
   the flow's transverse part (the meeting's reading, the first moment): V_perp = q Q b / (4 pi r^3) = -(Q / 3) dA / dy exactly (5.1): the SAME integrand as the age word's turn; a grain constant in place of f (n / d)

   b = 6 (per unit of n / d, f = 1; the crowd of one unit per direction per interval; A(b) on the lattice 21, the continuum's 11.5; P(b) 2, the continuum's 1.11):
     the age word:      the lattice turn via the flow, sum 3 V_y / Q over the path    78.28 rad; the closed form 2 k_a(b) L / sqrt(L^2 + b^2) =    22.49 (2 k_a(b) = 23.08); the neighbour difference -dA/dy summed   331.50 (not a field at this fan: the six neighbours lie on other lines or none)
     the presence word: the neighbour difference -dP/dy summed    12.50 (the same comb); the closed form pi k_s(b) ~     3.49
     the delay, the age word: sum A(x) / c_h =   2834.2 interval per unit n / d; the closed form (k_a(b) b / c) 2 asinh(L / b) =    521.0
     the delay, the presence word: sum P(x) / c_h =    116.9; the closed form pi k_s(b) b / c x (finite) ~     36.2
   b = 3 (per unit of n / d, f = 1; the crowd of one unit per direction per interval; A(b) on the lattice 29, the continuum's 23.1; P(b) 6, the continuum's 4.44):
     the age word:      the lattice turn via the flow, sum 3 V_y / Q over the path    98.91 rad; the closed form 2 k_a(b) L / sqrt(L^2 + b^2) =    45.85 (2 k_a(b) = 46.15); the neighbour difference -dA/dy summed  -420.00 (not a field at this fan: the six neighbours lie on other lines or none)
     the presence word: the neighbour difference -dP/dy summed    10.50 (the same comb); the closed form pi k_s(b) ~    13.95
     the delay, the age word: sum A(x) / c_h =   2201.7 interval per unit n / d; the closed form (k_a(b) b / c) 2 asinh(L / b) =    684.9
     the delay, the presence word: sum P(x) / c_h =    151.2; the closed form pi k_s(b) b / c x (finite) ~     72.5
   the b exponent from 6 to 3, the one number that decides light's word in the continuum: the age word's deflection doubles (1 / b), the presence word's quadruples (1 / b^2)
     on the lattice at series K's fan the flow sums give 1.26 from b = 6 to 3 (the register under the meeting: -2.30 at b = 3 against -1.79 at b = 6, DETECTOR; the offline flight -2.6 against -3.0): the beam lies in the mass's plane, section E

